  "raw_text": "A retry-on-invalid mechanism was introduced so that recoverable model failures are re-asked rather than silently dropped. The new call_and_validate routine calls the model, extracts and validates coordinates, and retries on validation errors or malformed output with a small temperature bump to break a stuck wrong answer, while never retrying genuine transport-down failures so that those stay fail-fast. The deeper rationale was that silently dropping an invalid small-model response had been starving the cross_scale step of needed scale tags; treating a recoverable miss as a missing dimension corrupted downstream results.",
